Switch: let the harness name the pipeline compile thread (aurora_switch_pipeline_thread_started)

The compile thread calls a weak hook when it starts. The Switch harness (thread_wrap.c) uses it
to report the thread's CPU time on its own and to keep it off the render worker's core, so that
during the loading screen and the warm-up the two never take turns on one core (Horizon does not
time-slice threads of equal priority). Without a definition nothing is called.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

--- a/lib/gfx/pipeline_cache.cpp	2026-10-04 12:48:10
+++ b/lib/gfx/pipeline_cache.cpp	2026-10-04 12:48:10
@@ -1104,11 +1104,17 @@
     g_warmupThrottleWaitNs += switch_stats::now_ns() - start;
   }
 }
+
+// Switch: the harness names this thread (its CPU time, and a core away from the render worker's).
+extern "C" __attribute__((weak)) void aurora_switch_pipeline_thread_started(void);
 
 static void pipeline_worker() {
 #ifdef TRACY_ENABLE
   tracy::SetThreadName("Pipeline compilation thread");
 #endif
+  if (aurora_switch_pipeline_thread_started != nullptr) {
+    aurora_switch_pipeline_thread_started();
+  }
 
   bool hasMore = false;
   while (g_hasPipelineThread || g_pipelinesPerFrame < BuildPipelinesPerFrame) {
